---
import { site } from "../../config/site";
import PlaceholderImage from "../PlaceholderImage.astro";
---

<section id="about" class="border-t border-line py-16 md:py-24">
  <div
    class="fade-in-section mx-auto grid max-w-[1100px] items-start gap-10 px-4 sm:px-6 md:grid-cols-[5fr_7fr] md:gap-14"
  >
    <PlaceholderImage
      alt={`${site.advisor.fullName} at work as a business broker`}
      ratio="4 / 5"
      class="max-w-[320px] justify-self-center md:max-w-none md:justify-self-start"
    />

    <div>
      <h2
        class="font-serif text-3xl font-semibold leading-tight tracking-tight sm:text-4xl"
      >
        About {site.advisor.name}
      </h2>
      <div class="mt-6 flex max-w-prose flex-col gap-5 text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
        <p>
          I'm a licensed business broker in Minneapolis at a national
          brokerage. I value small businesses, list them, qualify buyers, and
          get deals to close. The firm I work for sold over $1B in businesses
          last year, and our Minnesota office closed over $50M of it. I've
          seen every way a first-time buyer gets hurt. Almost all of them were
          avoidable.
        </p>
        <p>
          This started with my TikTok DMs. Smart people with money and work
          ethic, and no idea who to trust. Their options were a $15,000
          program or a $150,000 advisor, and most of that money pays for
          finding deals. There are plenty of deals. What buyers need is
          someone who knows what they're looking at.
        </p>
        <p>
          So this is that. No sourcing, no diligence, no cut. I sit next to
          you, tell you what I'd do, and keep you from spending money in the
          wrong order.
        </p>
      </div>
      <p class="mt-6 text-sm text-ink-soft">
        Licensed in Minnesota. Advisory clients anywhere in the US.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
